{"theory":"w-e7-coset","chiral_algebra":"\\mathcal{W}(E_7)_{13/10} = \\left((E_7)_1\\times(E_7)_2/(E_7)_3\\right)","Z_tex":"Z = \\sum_{(\\lambda,\\mu)/\\sim} |\\chi_{\\lambda,\\mu}|^2","character_tex":"Frenkel-Kac-Wakimoto characters $\\chi_{\\lambda,\\mu} = \\eta(\\tau)^{-7}\\sum_{w\\in W}\\epsilon(w)\\sum_{\\alpha\\in Q} q^{|p'(\\lambda+\\rho)-p\\,w(\\mu+\\rho)+pp'\\alpha|^2/2pp'}$ of $\\mathcal{W}(E_7)$ at $(p,p') = (20,21)$, with $\\lambda$ an integrable $(E_7)_{2}$ weight and $\\mu$ an integrable $(E_7)_{3}$ weight (both labelled by the dimension of the $\\mathfrak{e_7}$ irrep), $h_{\\lambda,\\mu} = \\frac{|p'(\\lambda+\\rho)-p(\\mu+\\rho)|^2-|\\rho|^2}{2pp'}$. Equivalently $\\chi_{\\lambda,\\mu}$ is the branching function of the $(E_7)_{3}$ module $\\mu$ in the $(E_7)_1\\times(E_7)_{2}$ module $\\nu\\otimes\\lambda$, the level-one label $\\nu$ being fixed by the conjugacy classes of $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$. Fields are identified as $(\\lambda,\\mu)\\sim(J\\lambda,J\\mu)$ under the $\\mathbb{Z}_2$ simple current, which acts freely on the 72 pairs because $(E_7)_3$ has no fixed points, leaving 36 fields (the level-2 fixed points $\\mathbf{56}$, $\\mathbf{912}$ are identified only through the level-3 label).","description":"Diagonal invariant of the coset $(E_7)_1\\times(E_7)_2/(E_7)_3$, the $\\mathcal{W}(E_7)$ minimal model (Bais-Bouwknegt-Surridge-Schoutens 1988; Frenkel-Kac-Wakimoto 1992). The affine Weyl orbit sum is done exactly by enumerating weight-lattice points in a ball and folding them into the level-21 alcove; the same code reproduces Rocha-Caridi and $\\mathcal{W}_3$ characters and independently computed $SU(4)$ and $SO(8)$ coset branching functions.","generator":"scripts/spectra/gen_exceptional_cosets.py","c":"13/10","irreducible":true,"cutoff":"4499/560","s_error":8.8e-16,"gap":"19/280","blocks":[{"label":"\\chi_{(\\mathbf{1};\\,\\mathbf{1})}","h":"0","coeffs":[1,0,1,1,2,2,5,5,10,12]},{"label":"\\chi_{(\\mathbf{56};\\,\\mathbf{56})}","h":"19/560","co